# Changelog and release audit trail

User-facing work is not done until `CHANGELOG.md` records it. Docs and GitHub
releases must stay in lockstep with that file.

- Add a Keep a Changelog bullet under `## [Unreleased]` in the same change as
  the behavior (Added / Changed / Fixed / Security). Do not leave a behavior
  PR with an empty Unreleased section.
- Never put secrets, bridge lines, onion/client keys, public IPs, local paths,
  or full command lines in changelog text or commit subjects.
- Before a version bump, move Unreleased into `## [x.y.z] - YYYY-MM-DD`, keep
  an empty `## [Unreleased]` on top, and run `make changelog-sync`. That writes
  [docs/reference/changelog.md](docs/reference/changelog.md) and the commit-subject
  page [docs/reference/release-audit.md](docs/reference/release-audit.md).
- `make check` and CI run `make changelog-check`. A stale generated docs page
  or a missing trail fails the build. Do not hand-edit the generated pages.
- GitHub release notes come from `scripts/extract-release-notes.mjs` (the dated
  CHANGELOG section). Do not invent a second marketing changelog.
- Releases stay alpha/prerelease until the stable gates in
  `docs/reference/release.md` pass. Do not call a 0.x build production-ready.
